  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/7061489c99c82c0348f3adb2cd379e8098435eb1</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/7061489c99c82c0348f3adb2cd379e8098435eb1"/>
    <title>
        feat(302ai): add gemini-4-argon (#10073)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-10-16T04:28:07Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82428497?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>JI4JUN</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/JI4JUN</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat(302ai): add gemini-4-argon (#10073)

Released 2026-10-13, featured on 302.AI. Lab metadata already on dev
(models/google/gemini-4-argon.toml), so this is a provider-only
override.

Pricing from the 302.AI catalog API and product page (cross-checked):
input $4, output $10, cache read $0.2, cache write $0.375 per MTok.

Reasoning options verified by live probe on api.302ai.cn: on the
OpenAI-compatible surface reasoning_effort/thinking_level/thinking_budget
are all silently ignored (invalid values also return 200, and a hard
reasoning task shows no token/answer difference across levels). On the
native Gemini surface (POST /v1beta/models/gemini-4-argon:generateContent)
generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel is validated server-side:
low/medium/high accepted with monotonic thoughtsTokenCount
(127 -&amp;gt; 450), while minimal/none/invalid are rejected. Matches the
level set of the existing gemini-3.6/3.7/3.8 entries.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
